decisions:
  - id: D-content-page-parser
    decision: Use simple regex-based markdown parser instead of MDX
    rationale: Keeps build fast, no heavy dependency, code stays understandable. The parser handles headings, code blocks, tables, lists, and inline formatting — covers 95% of doc needs.
  - id: D-dual-course-sources
    decision: Load courses from two directories — university package and site-local content
    rationale: Core PARA courses are a shared package used by the CLI university platform. Extracurricular courses are site-only content that doesn't need to ship in the npm package.
  - id: D-quiz-display-only
    decision: Display quiz questions inline without answer interaction
    rationale: The graded quiz experience belongs in the University platform (paradigm university serve). The site shows questions for review/study, not assessment.
learnings:
  - Auto-generated + handwritten docs is the right architecture — neither alone is sufficient
  - Sidebar filter is a small feature with outsized UX impact on large doc sets (1200+ pages)
  - Content verification caught a real error (non-existent CLI command) — always verify docs against codebase
  - Quiz format normalization (choices/correct vs options/answer) was needed because PARA and extracurricular courses evolved independently
