body: |-
  ## What changed

  This session took the site from "auto-generated symbol reference" to a real documentation + learning platform. The key additions:

  ### Library (Docs)
  - **Breadcrumbs** built from URL slugs — simple but makes navigation feel professional
  - **Sidebar filter** — live text narrowing, sections auto-hide when empty, filter disables collapse. Small feature, big UX impact.
  - **4 handwritten content pages** — These complement the auto-generated symbol pages. CLI Reference, Flows, MCP Tools, Portal & Gates. Verified against actual codebase (caught `paradigm flow validate` which doesn't exist as a CLI command).
  - **Code block language headers** — Code blocks with a language specifier get a styled header bar. Subtle polish.

  ### University (Learn)
  - **CourseDataLoader** — reads from two sources: core PARA courses (from `packages/university/`) and extracurricular courses (from `packages/site/src/content/courses/`). Normalizes different quiz formats (PARA uses `choices/correct`, extracurricular uses `options/answer`).
  - **Course overview pages** — syllabus with numbered lesson links, core vs extracurricular badges
  - **Lesson pages** — full markdown rendering (reuses ContentPage pattern but adds ordered lists and italic), key concepts sidebar, inline quiz display, prev/next navigation
  - **PLSAT page** — certification landing with coverage grid, exam stats, prep guide
  - **2 extracurricular courses** — Git Fundamentals and Agile Development, 6 lessons each with quizzes

  ### Infrastructure
  - **Platform server SPA fix** — API routes were being caught by the wildcard `sendFile(index.html)` fallback. Now `/api/*` routes pass through to `next()`.

  ## What's next

  The site is genuinely good now. Areas to expand:
  - **More handwritten docs** — Getting Started guide, Purpose Files deep-dive, Aspects guide
  - **Interactive elements** — Quiz taking with answer reveal, progress tracking
  - **Search** — Full-text search across docs + university content
  - **More extracurricular courses** — TypeScript patterns, testing strategies, CI/CD
  - **Blog content** — The Voice role is still empty
  - **Agents Registry** — The Armory role needs its marketplace UI

  ## Reflection

  The pattern of auto-generated docs (from scan-index) + handwritten guides (from markdown files) is the right architecture. Neither alone is sufficient — auto-generated gives completeness, handwritten gives narrative and teaching. The ContentPage markdown parser is deliberately simple (no MDX dependency) which keeps the build fast and the code understandable.
